# Build output. `go build` in the repository root drops the binary here, and
# the baseline build for the 2026-09-18 review left a 6.99 MB mkcert.exe
# untracked in the working tree -- reported by `git status` on every check, and
# one careless `git add -A` away from being committed into a repository whose
# entire purpose is controlling its own release artefacts.
#
# Leading slashes on purpose: a bare `mkcert` would also match a directory of
# that name at any depth.
/mkcert
/mkcert.exe

# Cross-compiled release artefacts, named mkcert-<version>-<goos>-<goarch>.
/mkcert-*

# Test binaries from `go test -c`.
*.test
*.test.exe

# Certificates and keys, in case anyone runs the tool from inside the checkout.
# Leaking a CA private key through a commit is not a recoverable mistake.
*.pem
*.p12
